.SH NAME
gyro-container-egress-approval-set - Approval step for egress changes


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container egress-approval set  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Approval step for egress changes

.PP
\fBhours\fR 1-72 turns the approval step on (24 recommended), 0 turns it off. Every change of a dedicated environment's node set (plan change, extra node added or removed) is announced BEFORE the old nodes go: as soon as the new nodes' addresses are known (usually under a minute) the owner is notified (Alerts channels, event \fBegress\fR) and \fBegress_change\fR / \fBpending_egress_ips\fR show them. With the approval step on (\fBPUT /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-approval\fR, 1-72 hours, 24 recommended) the new nodes take no traffic and the old nodes keep serving until \fBPOST /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-change/approve\fR or the deadline (then it continues by itself). A removal only never waits.

.PP
API: PUT /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-approval (operationId setContainerEgressApproval, scope services_write)


